provenance.prompt:
Create one original 1536×1024 true-transparent RGBA production sprite sheet for Moxie Capwell of Moonmorel Hex performing a right-facing one-handed layup. Use the supplied canon portrait and gameplay references. Moxie is an adult human woman with pale skin, lavender-purple eyes, a very long thick lavender high ponytail tied with a small gold tie, mature athletic proportions, purple-and-silver uniform with white side panels, purple wristbands and purple high-top shoes. Keep her face, eyes, hair, ponytail tie, kit and human anatomy consistent. No witch hat, beard, male, monster, robot or other character.

Draw crisp late-1990s arcade basketball sprite art with a clean outline, readable limbs and consistent scale. Exactly eight distinct complete full-body poses in a strict 4-column by 2-row grid, row-major; one pose per cell with broad alpha-zero gutters and outer margins. Never clip or overlap her ponytail, hands, feet or shoes. The basketball remains separate: never draw a ball, sphere, seams, hoop, rim, court, floor, shadow, glow, effect, text, labels, border, teammate or background. Both hands empty in all poses.

0 right-facing controlled approach toward the basket;
1 step and plant for a layup, eyes toward the target;
2 push off the outside foot and rise;
3 airborne, knees lift, shooting-side hand brings imaginary ball toward the head;
4 single layup RELEASE at the apex at simulation tick9, shooting arm reaches high toward an implied rim with open empty palm;
5 extended follow-through, guide arm balances and ponytail trails;
6 descend under control, legs begin to extend;
7 land with flexed knees and recover upright.

Use believable athletic takeoff and reach with full human limbs. Keep the high lavender ponytail/gold tie and face unobstructed by the shooting arm; do not put fingers into the hair. Show all eight poses distinct and connected. Return only clean true-transparent RGBA sprites, no checkerboard, haze, matte, speckles or halo.
